{
  "id": "worldwide-executive-job-search-solutions",
  "title": "Worldwide Executive Job Search Solutions / PrivateEquityHeadhunters.com",
  "typology": "job-scam",
  "period": "2019",
  "summary": "The FTC alleged that Worldwide Executive Job Search Solutions, PrivateEquityHeadhunters.com and owner Craig Chrest messaged job seekers on LinkedIn and other networking sites, claiming access to unadvertised executive jobs at private equity and venture capital firms. Consumers paid upfront fees of $1,200 to $2,500, but the interviews and jobs were fictitious. A federal court in the Southern District of Texas froze assets in February 2019, and an October 2019 settlement permanently banned the defendants from offering employment services, with a $1,744,422 judgment of which all but $18,000 was suspended.",
